                      Children:
                        - HtmlGeneralInformation_HelpText:
                            Control: HtmlViewer@2.1.0
                            Properties:
                              AutoHeight: =true
                              DisabledBorderColor: =RGBA(56, 56, 56, 1)
                              DisplayMode: =DisplayMode.View
                              Font: =Font.'Open Sans'
                              HtmlText: |-
                                ="<p><center><h2>Guidance Notes for Section About the Incident</h2></center></p>
                                <p><ul>
                                <li><b>Injury</b> - Any injuries (including stress)</li>
                                <li><b>Near Miss</b> - To include an incident that did not result in an injury but had the potential to cause an injury <b>e.g.</b> a chair that needs replacing as it has sharp edges or staples showing</li>
                                <li><b>Location</b> - Include details of site, exact location</li>
                                <li><b>Training</b> - Provide the title of the training event</li>
                                <li><b>Date Incident Occured</b> - This is the date and time the incident happened</li>
                                <li><b>Date Incident Reported to CNC H&S</b> - this is the date and time that the incident is reported to the CNC H&S</li>
                                <li><b>Description of Incident</b> - This section should give details of what led up to the incident.</li></ul></p>
                                <p>Include any contributing factors, any equipment being used, and any contact with hazardous substances <b>e.g.</b> <em>'During a routine foot patrol of the perimeter fence at Sellafield, I lost my footing and slipped over. The ground was dry at the time and I could see no hazards. At the time I felt pain in my left knee and had to attend on site occupational health. I later returned to my duties. At the time of the incident I was wearing my full body armour and Tac vest.'</em></p>
                                <p>If you feel that it is necessary to include diagrams, photographs that will give more clarity of the description given, please include them in Section Attachments.</p>
                                <p><b>Remember: Only provide the facts (do not include personal opinions).</b></p>
                                <ul><li><b>Witnesses</b> - This section muls also provide the names and contact details of anyone who witnessed the incident. Please include name, rank and if appropriate collar number. A contactable email address or telephone number should also be provided.</li></ul>"
